{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"usesSigns","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sign"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/usesSigns","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/usessigns"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether Ped, Sost, and * signs are used.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPedalV9usesSignsSbSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"usesSigns","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"usesSigns","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/usesSigns":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether Ped, Sost, and * signs are used."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/usessigns","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"usesSigns"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"usesSigns","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/usesSigns"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal","abstract":[{"text":"The pedal type represents piano pedal marks, including damper and sostenuto pedal marks. The line attribute is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yes if pedal lines are used. The sign attribute is yes if Ped, Sost, and * signs are used. For compatibility","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with older versions, the sign attribute is yes by default if the line attribute is no, and is no by default if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the line attribute is yes. If the sign attribute is set to yes and the type is start or sostenuto, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"abbreviated attribute is yes if the short P and S signs are used, and no if the full Ped and Sost signs are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used. It is no by default. Otherwise the abbreviated attribute is ignored. The alignment attributes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored if the sign attribute is no."}],"title":"MXLPedal","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPedal","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPedal","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}